# Python docstring layout

Put the opening `"""` on its own line. Start the docstring text on the next line.
Close with `"""` on its own line. Applies to module, class, function, method, and
attribute docstrings.

```python
# BAD
"""Short summary on the same line as the opener."""

"""Summary starts on the opener line.

More detail…
"""

# GOOD
"""
Short summary.
"""

"""
Summary on its own line.

More detail…
"""
```

Do not reformat non-docstring triple-quoted literals (e.g. `INSTRUCTIONS = """\…`).
